; TEST: expect-exit=2
;
; A `br` whose two targets are ONE block with a phi. That gives b1 two edges
; from b0, so its phi has two pairs naming b0 -- one per edge, in edge
; order: the true edge first, then the false one (ssa-ir.md section 2.4).
; Which pair an edge reads cannot be decided by the predecessor's block id
; alone; emit.inc's `__bfa_phi_operand` takes a `skipn`, and the false
; edge's stub passes 1 when both targets agree.
;
; 2 lt 1 is false, so the false edge runs and the phi must read its SECOND
; b0 pair: 2. An emitter that matched only on the block id reads the first
; pair on both edges and exits 1.
;
; The lowering never builds this shape -- every `br` it emits has two
; distinct targets -- but the IR permits it and the verifier accepts it, so
; the emitter must not get it wrong silently.
;
; `-> u64` for tier1_combo_lt.ir's reason.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u64 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u64 1
%2 = iconst u64 2
%3 = cmp.lt u64 %2 %1
br %3 b1 b1
b1:
%4 = phi u64 b0 %1 b0 %2
ret %4
}
